# P15 (docs/phase15-brief.md 3.3, 7): pause and resume fade through the
# index-based table (apps/ipodui/fadecurve.h, 25 steps). pcmbuf.c logs
# "ipodui: fade dir=in|out steps=<n>" when a fade starts, n = the ticks
# left to run it: 25 from silence or full volume, fewer when it turns
# around part-way. Here the queue is paused, then resumed while the
# fade-out still runs, so the second line is "dir=in" with steps < 25 (a
# reversal from where the level is, not a restart); check_trace.py's
# p15fade rule checks 0 <= steps <= 25 for every line and, with
# "# fade: reverse", that an opposite-direction line has 0 < steps < 25.
# A later, unhurried pause/resume pair shows two full 25-step fades.
# Timing-sensitive: how far the first fade got depends on the machine, so
# the shots are not goldens.
#   SIM_BUILD=build/sim-ui scripts/shots.sh tests/ui/ipodui-p15-fade.script
# needs: music
# timeout: 90
# trace: p15fade
# fade: reverse
# logbetween: calm end dir=out steps=25
# logbetween: calm end dir=in steps=25
# fulls-extra: 1 the main menu redraws in full when its Now Playing row appears
# golden: skip turned settled

wait 3000
repeat off
wait_db 30000
play_files /Music/Tone%20Collective/Sine%20Studies/01%20Concert%20A.mp3
wait_pos 3000 20000 Concert
key PLAY 30         # pause: the fade-out starts
wait 120            # a part of the fade-out has run
key PLAY 30         # resume mid-fade: the fade-in turns it around
wait 2500
shot turned
ab_mark calm
key PLAY 30         # pause and let it settle
wait 3000
shot settled
key PLAY 30         # resume from silence
wait 2000
quit
